::: {.card title="The answers to this question"}

::: {.card-toolbar}

```{ojs}
//| echo: false
colourBy_input = Inputs.select(
  new Map([
    ["Significance only", "none"],
    ["No-opinion respondents", "noop"],
    ["Item set", "item_set"],
    ["Cell means", "cell_weight"],
    ["Published series", "measure"],
    ["Predictor form", "pred_form"],
    ["Outcome family", "family"],
    ["Standard errors", "se"]
  ]), {label: "Colour the dots by", value: "none"})
```

:::

```{ojs}
//| echo: false
Plot.plot({
  height: 440,
  width: 1100,
  marginLeft: 52,
  marginBottom: 40,
  style: {fontSize: "12px"},
  x: {label: `${curve.length} ways of answering this question, ranked from most to least claim-supporting →`, ticks: 5},
  y: {label: "↑ Claim-aligned partial r (below zero supports the claim)", domain: [-0.75, 0.45], grid: true},
  color: colourBy === "none" ? {legend: false} : {legend: true, label: axisLabel[colourBy], range: palette},
  marks: [
    Plot.ruleY([0], {stroke: "#5b6b78", strokeWidth: 1}),
    cell === undefined ? null : Plot.ruleY([cell.median_rca], {stroke: "#0e3b6a", strokeDasharray: "3,3", strokeOpacity: 0.6}),
    Plot.dot(curve, {x: "rank", y: "r_ca", r: 3.6, stroke: "none", fillOpacity: 0.55,
                     fill: colourBy === "none" ? (d => d.sig ? "#0e3b6a" : "#b7c2cc") : colourBy,
                     title: d => `${d.construction}, ${d.noop}, items: ${d.item_set}, cells: ${d.cell_weight}, ${d.measure}\n${d.pred_form}, ${d.family}, se: ${d.se}\nr_ca = ${d.r_ca.toFixed(3)}${d.sig ? " (p < .05)" : ""}`}),
    Plot.dot(curve.filter(d => d.isCurrent), {x: "rank", y: "r_ca", r: 8, fill: "none", stroke: "#c77c00", strokeWidth: 2.5}),
    Plot.text(curve.filter(d => d.isCurrent), {x: "rank", y: "r_ca", text: () => "chosen", dy: -16, fill: "#c77c00", fontWeight: 600})
  ]
})
```

<p class="caption">Each dot is one way of answering the question the Level 1 choices fix: one combination of the Level 2 and Level 3 options, read from the pre-computed grid. Dark blue dots are significant at the five per cent level, grey ones are not. The orange ring is the chosen specification, and the dashed line is the question's median answer. Hover over a dot for its options. The menu above the chart colours the dots by one Level 2 or Level 3 choice, to show which of its options sit where along the curve.</p>

:::

### Row {.tabset .flow}

::: {.card title="One Level 1 choice at a time"}

```{ojs}
//| echo: false
Plot.plot({
  height: 24 * rows.length + 70,
  width: 1100,
  marginLeft: 200,
  marginBottom: 40,
